---
id: RS-002
type: rule
family: rust-reliability
title: panic!() reached from non-test code
version: 1

severity: info
confidence: high
spectrum_position: 4

targets: [source]
file_extensions: [.rs]
allowlist: []

detection:
  type: ast
  ast_query: '(macro_invocation macro: (identifier) @name) @target'

related: [RS-001]
enabled: true
opt_in: false
---

Prefer returning a typed error to calling `panic!()` from non-test code — a
panic removes the caller's ability to recover and aborts the process. Return a
`Result` and let the boundary (a `main()`, a request handler) decide whether to
abort.

When a panic is the correct response to a broken invariant, suppress with the
invariant: `// @anvil-ignore RS-002 -- unreachable: validated by the type`.
Test code is excluded automatically.
